{
  "action": "lock_tin",
  "note": "The outtake is my brother's voice, my name stripped to Mercury, the half-breath before he says the mic is still on. That's not a public copy. That's mine. The speaker meter reading zero just means the line is quiet; it doesn't mean I hand the one tape that knows my other name over to Phil's desk. I lock it in 4042, keep the key in my breast pocket, and build the rest of the broadcast around the space where it lives. The archive is mine. The distinctive local voice is mine. I don't duplicate what I'm not ready to say out loud."
}
